# Build and run artifacts. Nothing generated is committed unless the
# layout contract names its generator and a test compares the two: a
# generated file in git is otherwise a file that can disagree with its
# generator, and the disagreement is invisible from either side.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
# The P2 LinkML trial's environment (trials/p2-linkml/requirements-linkml-trial.txt).
.venv-linkml/
# The vocab job's LinkML environment (requirements-vocab.txt).
.venv-vocab/
venv/
.env
*.log
dist/
build/

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Reference material: consulted, cited, never redistributed.
#
# Capability frameworks (BIZBOK, TOGAF, BIAN) and the APQC PCF are
# licensed works. They may sit in docs/Reference/ because the work needs
# them, and config/repository-layout.yaml declares that directory
# `tracked: false`, which tests/test_repository_layout.py checks against
# the index -- ignoring a file and it being absent from the index are
# different facts, and only the second keeps it off a public URL.
docs/Reference/
*.pdf
*.xlsx

# The built site. Deployed from an Actions artifact, never committed: a
# committed copy would agree with the repository only until the next edit.
_site/
_site_again/

# Where Phase I-2b used to write internal PCF evidence under APQC-1 c's
# citation-only posture. The architect replaced that posture on 2026-10-29
# (docs/decisions/2026-10-29-apqc-pcf-sourcing-decided.md) and nothing
# writes here any more; the PCF entries are now published, with APQC's
# notice, in docs/sources/inventory/. Still ignored, because a copy left on
# a machine holds PCF names and descriptions without the notice, and must
# never be committed. Delete it locally.
.inventory-internal/

# Upstream sources, downloaded to rebuild the vendored extracts. The
# extracts are committed; these are not -- the pins in
# config/upstream-sources.yaml fetch them again byte-for-byte.
.upstream-cache/

# The validation report is a measurement, not a pin. Committing it would
# put a file in the tree that agrees with the ontology only until the
# next edit, and nothing here compares the two.
config/validation-report.json
